19 Del. C. § 1102

§ 1102. Minimum wage rate.

(a) Except as may otherwise be provided under this chapter, every employer shall pay to each employee in any occupation wages of a rate not less than the rates set forth in this section.

(b) Upon the effective date of this subsection, the minimum wage shall be as follows:

(1) Beginning January 1, 2022, the minimum wage shall be not less than $10.50 per hour;

(2) Beginning January 1, 2023, the minimum wage shall be not less than $11.75 per hour;

(3) Beginning January 1, 2024, the minimum wage shall be not less than $13.25 per hour;

(4) Beginning January 1, 2025, the minimum wage shall be not less than $15.00 per hour.

13 Pa.C.S. § 2314

§ 2314. Implied warranty: merchantability; usage of trade.

(a) Sale by merchant.--Unless excluded or modified (section 2316), a warranty that the goods shall be merchantable is implied in a contract for their sale if the seller is a merchant with respect to goods of that kind. Under this section the serving for value of food or drink to be consumed either on the premises or elsewhere is a sale.

(b) Merchantability standards for goods.--Goods to be merchantable must be at least such as:

(1) pass without objection in the trade under the contract description;

(3) are fit for the ordinary purposes for which such goods are used;
